==Ladin==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|lld|la|dāre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|dō|t=give}}.

===Verb===
{{head|lld|verb}}

# {{lb|lld|Gherdëina, Badiot}} to [[give]] (changing ownership)
#: {{syn|lld|scinché}}
#: {{uxi|lld|Mi fëna me à '''dat''' na nueva ëura..|My wife '''gave''' me a new watch.}}
# {{lb|lld|Gherdëina, Badiot}} to [[hand]], to [[pass]], to put within reach
#: {{uxi|lld|'''Da''' me chël!|'''Give''' me that!}}
#: {{uxi|lld|'''Da''' me la man.|'''Give''' me your hand (to hold).}}
#: {{uxi|lld|Pos'a me '''dé''' chëla biro?|Could you '''hand''' me that pen?}}
# {{lb|lld|Gherdëina, Badiot}} {{ngd|Used to indicate that something exists (often with a certain property and/or in a certain location). Usually translated as {{m|en|there be|there is/are}} or {{m|en|there exist|there exist(s)}}}}
#: {{uxi|lld|'''Dal''' pa de bona scoles tlo ntëur?|'''Are''' there good schools in the neighborhood?}}
#: {{uxi|lld|L ne '''da''' deguna ega tl desert.|There '''is''' no water in this desert.}}
#: {{uxi|lld|Chësc ne '''dal''' pu nia!|This is nothing that could possibly '''exist'''!}}
# {{lb|lld|Gherdëina, Badiot}} to communicate (helpful information such as a hint or advice), to [[signal]] (in a certain way such as a sign)
#: {{uxi|lld|Possi pa te '''dé''' n cunsëi?|May I '''give''' you some advice?}}
#: {{uxi|lld|L jugadëur à '''dat''' n signal che l ulova unì mudà ora.|The player '''gave''' a signal that he wanted to be substituted.}}
# {{lb|lld|Gherdëina, Badiot}} to [[present]]; to [[put]]
# {{lb|lld|Gherdëina, Badiot}} to result in

